/-! ## Negative control: value asymptotics do not give derivative control

`x ↦ 1 + x⁷ sin((x⁸)⁻¹)` on `(0, ∞)` has value remainder `O(x⁷)`: **every** value coefficient
below order 7 is that of the constant `1`. Its actual derivative, however, is
`7x⁶ sin(x⁻⁸) − 8x⁻² cos(x⁻⁸)` (the outer `x⁷` cancels one power of `x` in `x¹⁴/x¹⁶`), whose
second term grows like `x⁻²` and oscillates in sign, so the derivative has no finite right limit
at `0⁺`. The no-limit conclusion itself is an analysis argument (`notes/VII16_ASYMPTOTIC_ANALYSIS.md`
§6); only the two algebraic facts above are formalised in Lean.

This function is **not** an Einstein–Maxwell solution. It refutes only the inference
"value expansion ⇒ differentiable control", which is precisely the inference the paper's
Eq. (30)/(33) do not license and which `FiniteBranch6` requires. -/

end ExactVacuumAtlas.EinsteinMaxwell.ES5.KerrSchild.VII16

